 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "The wind is born again.\nA carpet of white snows, like flowers,\nWhispers in the nightingales' voices\nWhere the endless towers,\nSwayed by midnight's swift-stirred wind,\nBeat on to their thousand-carpet walls;\nAnd the quiet laughter of flowers\nSound like a storm-cloud falling falls,\nMore than stillness.    There somewhere,\nIn thy weary meditation,\nThy whisper-brooding heart may somewhere\nBut thine; it would be lonely been",
